From: McKernel Rust Migration <mckernel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] objtool: recognize Rust 1.92 sort and Vec removal panics
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0000

Rocky-Base: linux-6.12.0-211.44.1.el10_2
Observed-Rustc: 1.92.0
License: GPL-2.0-only

Native memory ownership uses Rust slice sorting and Vec::remove. Their emitted
panic calls end at padding before the next function, which objtool currently
rejects as fallthrough. The exact Rust 1.92 library defines both
core::slice::sort::shared::smallsort::panic_on_ord_violation and the nested
alloc::vec::Vec::remove::assert_failed with return type ! and panic bodies.

Recognize only the two observed mangled path suffixes, independent of their
crate disambiguators. Keep all existing control-flow checks and reject unknown
callees. This is a project-observed compatibility adjustment; no upstream or
stable commit is claimed.

Signed-off-by: McKernel Rust Migration <mckernel@localhost>
---
 tools/objtool/check.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/objtool/check.c b/tools/objtool/check.c
--- a/tools/objtool/check.c
+++ b/tools/objtool/check.c
@@ -207,6 +207,8 @@ static bool is_rust_noreturn(const struct symbol *func)
 	 */
 	return str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core5sliceSp15copy_from_slice17len_mismatch_fail")		||
+	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core5slice4sort6shared9smallsort22panic_on_ord_violation")	||
+	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_5alloc3vecINtB6_3VecppE6remove13assert_failed")		||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core6option13unwrap_failed")				||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core6result13unwrap_failed")				||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core9panicking5panic")					||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core9panicking9panic_fmt")					||
